---
import DocLayout from '../layouts/DocLayout.astro';
---

<DocLayout title="Keyboard Shortcuts">
  <h1>Keyboard Shortcuts & Modals</h1>
  <p>
    Scene Light Manager leverages interactive viewport modal operators. These let you transform lights, rotate environment maps, and adjust parameters directly in the 3D Viewport using fluid mouse gestures and hotkeys.
  </p>

  <hr class="my-8 border-white/5" />

  <h2>── 1. Viewport Hotkeys ──</h2>
  <p>
    These shortcuts are registered globally in Blender and are active during standard 3D Viewport navigation:
  </p>

  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-8">
    <div class="bg-white/[0.02] border border-white/5 p-5 rounded-2xl flex flex-col gap-3">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
        <strong class="text-white text-sm">Quick Properties Popup</strong>
        <span class="px-2.5 py-1 rounded bg-amber-500/10 text-amber-400 border border-amber-500/20 font-mono text-xs font-semibold">Y</span>
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed font-light">
        Opens a floating settings card under the mouse cursor. Access exposure, color temperature, and texture presets immediately without needing properties tabs open.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-white/[0.02] border border-white/5 p-5 rounded-2xl flex flex-col gap-3">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
        <strong class="text-white text-sm">Rotate Sun & HDRI</strong>
        <span class="px-2.5 py-1 rounded bg-amber-500/10 text-amber-400 border border-amber-500/20 font-mono text-xs font-semibold">Ctrl + Alt + RMB</span>
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed font-light">
        Enters a modal state. Drag the mouse left/right to rotate world environment coordinates, sun mapping directions, or Cycles HDRI textures in real-time.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <hr class="my-8 border-white/5" />

  <h2>── 2. Modal Operator Modifiers ──</h2>
  <p>
    While executing a modal operator (such as rotating HDRI or dragging spatial sliders), use these modifier keys to refine adjustments:
  </p>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th class="w-1/3">Key Modifier</th>
        <th>Action Effect</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><strong class="text-white">Hold Shift</strong></td>
        <td><strong>Precision Mode:</strong> Drastically decreases mouse sensitivity. Ideal for fine-tuning exposure levels by decimal values.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong class="text-white">Hold Ctrl</strong></td>
        <td><strong>Stepped Snapping:</strong> Restricts parameter adjustments to fixed increments (e.g., increments of 15° for rotation or 1.0 for exposure).</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong class="text-white">Left Click / Enter</strong></td>
        <td><strong>Confirm Changes:</strong> Validates and saves the active modifications, ending the modal viewport session.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong class="text-white">Right Click / Escape</strong></td>
        <td><strong>Cancel Changes:</strong> Discards all shifts, reverting the values back to their pre-modal state.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <hr class="my-8 border-white/5" />

  <h2>── 3. Customizing Shortcuts ──</h2>
  <p>
    If you have conflicting addons or prefer alternative keymaps, you can customize the keybindings inside the addon preferences (<strong>Edit &gt; Preferences &gt; Keymap</strong>):
  </p>

  <ul class="space-y-4 mb-6 text-xs font-mono">
    <li class="bg-white/[0.01] border border-white/5 p-3 rounded-lg flex flex-col gap-1">
      <span class="text-white font-semibold">k_tools.quick_popup</span>
      <span class="text-zinc-500">Triggers the floating properties card (Default: Y).</span>
    </li>
    <li class="bg-white/[0.01] border border-white/5 p-3 rounded-lg flex flex-col gap-1">
      <span class="text-white font-semibold">k_tools.rotate_hdri</span>
      <span class="text-zinc-500">Enters the modal environment rotation session (Default: Ctrl + Alt + RMB).</span>
    </li>
    <li class="bg-white/[0.01] border border-white/5 p-3 rounded-lg flex flex-col gap-1">
      <span class="text-white font-semibold">k_tools.light_at_point</span>
      <span class="text-zinc-500">Projects a spotlight target coordinate straight to the cursor surface intersection point.</span>
    </li>
  </ul>
</DocLayout>
